  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_hawks_hood_cb0">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>hawk's hood, a covering of leather put over the head of a hawk to blind her when not pursuing game (OED s.v. hood n.1 4) | (OED s.v. hawk n.1 4) no definition, but a quote from 1483: hawkesbagge, cassidile, exact meaning unknown | hawk’s hood, a covering of leather put over the head of a hawk to blind her when not pursuing game (OED s.v. hood n.^1 4)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
